 "about_text": "Maki Fine Arts is a contemporary art gallery in Tokyo, founded in the fall of 2010 by director Takahiro Maki. The gallery originally opened in Chuo-ku and relocated in 2015 to its current space in Kagurazaka, Shinjuku-ku. Its program represents a group of Japanese and international artists working across painting, sculpture, and mixed media, and the gallery regularly participates in art fairs in Japan and abroad, including NADA New York, Art Fair Tokyo, and Art Collaboration Kyoto. Represented artists have also been featured in institutional exhibitions at museums such as the Museum of Contemporary Art Tokyo and the National Museum of Modern Art, Tokyo.",
